That's the Philips/LMSI CM100, which DEC apparently rebadged as an RRD50.
Uses a DA15 connector, with two EIA-422 pairs from the controller to the
drive, and two more pairs from the drive back to the controller.  I
disassembled and mostly commented the firmware from the drive.  But I've
never been able to find one of DEC's controllers for the thing, which
were apparently the M7490 for Unibus, and the M7552 (KRQ50) for Qbus.


