Did you type >>> B dka500 (where dka500 is the cd rom devi name), without
boot flags?
Because the boot flags for unix are different from VMS and are kept by srm.
Re-enter the nvram data (they don't harm the system: it will still boot WNT)
and type

>>> b -fl 0,0 dka500

The system did find a valid boot block on the CD so it's worth a try.

