As bad as the engineering practice sounds, a very low resistance, low
wattage resistor was frequently used as a replacement for a fuse with
the understanding that if the current draw expected for the fuse was
exceeded, like the fuse it would blow.  It may rub many the wrong way,
but it is definitely better than using a smal piece of wire, which is
much closer to that analogy of a "a penny in the fuse box".

