switch
> for something?!

Sure, see above!

> A small gray port cover with the number 6 on it is labeled as "Bus 0."

Like SCSI, DSSI uses bus id's for connected devices; it uses the same range,
0..7 for device id's. The controller has its own ID, in this case it is set
to 6.

> Bus 1 has a similar gray cover, but the number 7.  It also seems to have
two
