>
> There are also three modular plugs.  "MO" "SI" and "SO"  what are these?
I
> haven't run across any reference to these in my (one short night of )
research.

These connectors were meant to control the power on sequence for expansion
cabinets. The VAXserver 4000's were typically sold as two node clusters.
Imagine two 4300's with two disk cabinets in between. Each DSSI bus would
connect to one disk cabinet and both VAXes. So the other VAX would have
those two grey plugs labeled 6 and 7 in exactly opposite positions. One
could then build shadow sets: each disk in the left disk cabinet would have
a counterpart in the other cabinet. Hi availability at a reasonable
(compared to VAX 6000's HSC90's and RA disks) price.

