With just a PC164 board in an old PC case (a SNI one...) I have a
similar problem, in that the DEC Alpha boards do not use the PS ON line
of the ATX powersupplies (neither use them nor provide the proper
signals). And the normal power button of an ATX case is just momentary,
and not a real switch as required by the ATX PSON signal.

So, I'd guess that there is something 'special' wrt. to the power supply
of the PWS (additional cables going to the front panels). Siemens PCs
also have this 'private' stuff, too.

> By the way, isn't there an option for the powersuppley to go on
> instantley? Technicalley, this would not be so difficult and for a
> server it would make sense. But something like that will be inside the
> PS...

So... just bridging the PSON pin of the ATX connector to GND will
probably be enough for an 'instant on' setup. That's actually what I
use, since the ATX power supply has an additional rocker switch at the
back. And the bridge ... is just a short piece of solder wire, plugged
in cable side of the ATX plug....

