Nathan Bloom wrote:
> 
> Hi,
> 
> I picked up a DEC AlphaPC164 Motherboard.  I am trying to set it up, but
> cannot determine were the power switch jumper is on this board.  Any help
> would be gratly appreciated.

Very simple: There is NONE. This board (and many others from DEC, too)
does not have the logic to control the PSON line of the ATX connector
from that momentary power 'switch' of an ATX case. 

If your power supply has a separate 'real' line switch, you can just
bridge the PSON with a GND pin on the ATX connector, or look for some
ideas similar to what Frank Arnold just wrote in the '[PWS 433au] How to
autopoweron ?' thread.
Or... have a more sophisticated power supply that has the necessary
logic integrated and a separate cable to a frontpanle or such, like the
DEC power supplies apparently had.

