You need to put two lines in nvram.
On the >>> prompt type ls
You get a listing of files, one of them is called nvram
Next : edit nvram
IIRC the appropriate command to add lines is the I (insert) command. The
editor behaves like an early ms-dos basic editor. Add these lines:

10 set boot_reset on
20 set srm_boot on

Exit the editor with control-Z. Power off, wait a minute, power on and boot
from the VMS distribution CD.

