There was a Tabletop CD-ROM drive, opened the top and dropped the CD-ROM on
the spindle. It had a serial interface of some kind to a board.

There was a Philips CD-ROM with proprietary carrier. You took the carrier
apart, inserted the CD-ROM and then resealed the unit. You inserted the
entire assembly into an RRD40 disk drive, I own one, and then you pulled
out, the front half of the carrier stayed in, the back half came out. Of
course, the CD-ROM stayed in too. Removal was the same process.

