Is the SCSI bus terminated?

Is the Standard I/O board jumper J6 installed?  If so, it will display a
FAIL I/O_00 message.  It should also be displaying a ash> prompt.  Power
down and remove the jumper.

Jumpers:
J3 - Power supply mode: when installed, dual power supplies operate in
redundant mode. When removed, operates in Full Power mode.  Default =
removed
J5 - Program voltage: DEC internal use only
J6 - Fail-Safe: When installed, selects the fail-safe loader firmware.
Enables you to power up without initializing drivers or running power-up
diagnostics

Did you try hitting the halt button (upside down triangle in a circle) to
see if you get a Chevron prompt?  See if you can test the system:  >>>  TEST
<CR>
>>>Show config

Check LEDs:
Power supply: Top is AC OK.  Bottom is DC OK


