>

In short - you don't. The Decserver 300 is a LAT device and, to the best of
my knowledge, doesn't support TCP/IP (telnet is a TCP/IP protocol) at all.
It does support what some have called "reverse LAT", where the output of a
LAT port is used to connect to a computer, instead of being used as an input
for a terminal. I do this with my Decserver 300, and this allows one
terminal to connect to the console ports of all my servers, on a
one-at-a-time basis.

Stuart Johnson




