Richard Hammersley wrote:
> 
> I'm looking for documentation for setting up a Decserver 300.
> 
> Specifically, how to set up reverse telnet.

Well, for any TCP/IP capable DECserver, you set up the port for remote
or dynamic access as your needs require, then use CHANGE PORT x TELNET
commands to assign the inbound socket number (TELNET "listener") for
that port. I don't have the exact syntax handy, but you'll find the
command level HELP useful. You may need to enable privilege to view the
appropriate HELP levels for changing a port's characteristics.

Of course, you'll have to set the server's IP address, etc. at the
CHANGE SERVER level. 

("CHANGE" does both DEFINE and SET at the same time, but doesn't work
for all object characteristics. For some, you'll need to DEFINE, then
reboot the server.)

Hope this helps...

(The technique for Xyplex servers is similar, but differs in important
ways.)

