There are two ways to connect to a port on a server. The "nicer" way is to
define a service on the port, then on VMS type "SET HOST/LAT <service>"

Sadly, this way doesn't work on the 90L+ as far as I know, so instead you
need to connect to a specified port.

SET HOST/LAT /NODE=<nodename_of_90L+> /DESTINATION_PORT=PORT_<n>

where n is the port number. This assumes (I can't check) that the ports on a
90L+ are called PORT_1 to PORT_8.

In both cases you will have to have set the port up for access. On the 90L+
you need to use the rather clunky menu. You need ACCESS=REMOTE, disable
autobaud, and set the desired speed. I can't remember which other settings
are possible - it's a rather limited subset of the more advanced servers.

I have a feeling you can do this remotely, maybe it's SET HOST/MOP to get to
the command prompt. If not, you need to connect a terminal.

This all works better on the 90M if you can get hold of one.

