Ah, that's what you want. The DS300 does support telnet, but connects to
another host, not vice versa as reverse-LAT does. The DS300 may be used to
connect to a printer and the VMS telnet symbiont and queue manager can use
that set up.
To configure IP on the DS300 make yourself privileged on the DS300. Try Help
INTERNET and it will tell you what to do: set up an address, a mask and a
default gateway and optionally a nameserver.
The trick here is that once you've made a type then the DEFINE command does
not override previously DEFINED
values, you've got to use the CHANGE INTERNET <attribute> command.
The built-in HELP is quite good.

Hans



