Properly configured, Kermit can transmit data at nearly the full speed
of the serial line.  At 9600 bps, 960 bytes/sec, you can transmit a
megabyte in about 18 minutes.  100 megabytes in a day and a quarter.

It would probably take more time than that to set up another transfer
scheme that might run faster.

