> I have a couple of IBM 9.1GB hard drives that i just picked up, and i wanted
> to put one in this DEC Workstation which is using a QLogic PCI SCSI Host
> adapter with 68 Pin connectors.

"DEC workstation" is a bit vague. Since you say Qlogic PCI controller,
this should be an Alpha with PCI bus. If the disk comes with 68pin 
connector (UW/U2W) there should be no problem. IBM disks can be jumpered
to single ended mode if the controller does not support LVD.

I run a DS10 with 2 36GB IBM disks plus KGPSA into the shared storage.
No problem.  My PWS500 works with IBM and Seagate disks.

Wolfgang Rupp



