The DE500 interface is a 10/100 uTP ethernet controller. Furthermore there
is
a combined SCSI/Ethernet interface, the KZPCM, with UTP that does 10/100
Mb/s as well.
Note that only a VMS branded KZPCM will work with VMS, the NT variant will
fail
with a CHECKSUM error.
The DE500 is a very simple PCI interface and probably not expensive and may
even be present in both systems.

My problem with the 5000 was that it had UTP only, all my other systems use
thinwire ethernet!
If you go for the 5000 and want to run VMS on it, you must modify the nvram
file. Google lists
the proper incantations, if you cannot find them send me an email.

