I haven't yet encountered a situation in which a virus trashed the HDD logic
board, altho it may well be possible if the logic board uses writable flash
memory for its controller program.

If you do not have an EXACT match between old and new HDD logic boards, there
may well be the possibility that the logic board has renamed the directories and
program names.  If that is what happened, then the DATA copied by Ghost would
also be corrupted, not just program and directory names.

Also, if there is not an EXACT match between old and new HDD logic boards, it
would be surprising that the hard drive would be accessable at all.  At least
that has been my limited experience.

