Look under /var/log, and see if that is what is using up all
of your root space. If so, you might want to look into a
program called 'logrotate' and see if you can make use of
it, or something similiar.

Also look at /tmp. Files should not be perminately allocated
there, so see if anything there is old.

Something must be consuming space, otherwise it wouldn't be
disappearing. You should determine where it is going, and
probably make changes to the system based on that. Otherwise
you will be continually fighting the same problem over and
over.




